on/octet-stream","state":"uploaded","size":188,"digest":"sha256:937039178a47cc43df6208504dc22da2d2a5de3cd1d73023a32d6d16b0813f0f","download_count":0,"created_at":"2026-10-16T19:12:31Z","updated_at":"2026-10-16T19:12:32Z","browser_download_url":"https://github.com/menudoproblema/mongoeco/releases/download/v4.10.1/SHA256SUMS"}],"tarball_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/menudoproblema/mongoeco/tarball/v4.10.1","zipball_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/menudoproblema/mongoeco/zipball/v4.10.1","body":"Mongoeco 4.10.1 corrects error documents, validation timing and BSON preservation in the supported MongoDB subset.\n\n- Complete `findAndModify` command errors and duplicate-key metadata; retain native exception families and classic/bulk envelopes.\n- Consolidate shared preparation and error transport, preserving error codes, counters, the first command failure and allowed partial writes.\n- Correct the exercised expression, array-filter, projection, schema, index and cursor paths. Preserve Binary subtypes, JavaScript scopes and SQLite NaN values through writes and reopening.\n- Expand the finite native MongoDB 7/8/9 corpus across direct/wire sync/async APIs and Memory/SQLite, including recovery and connection reuse.\n\nPublic API signatures, Engine SPI v2 and existing SQLite files remain compatible; no storage migration is required. Tests relying on invalid accepted operations or incomplete diagnostics may need updated expectations. This finite corpus does not claim universal MongoDB compatibility or identical wording for every error.\n\nThe distribution includes the ICU notice for its collation diagnostic resource and declares `Apache-2.0 AND ICU`.\n\nInstall: `python -m pip install mongoeco==4.10.1` (or `mongoeco[pytest]==4.10.1`).\n\n[Release notes and validation](https://github.com/menudoproblema/mongoeco/blob/main/docs/release-4.10.1.md) · [Changelog](https://github.com/menudoproblema/mongoeco/blob/main/CHANGELOG.md#4101---2026-10-16)\n\nValidation: 43,982 tests passed per Python 3.13/3.14/3.15, 99.01% installed coverage, native MongoDB 7/8/9 and the twelve pytest/PyMongo kit cells approved. Clean public installation, regression checks and Memory/SQLite SPI v2 conformance also passed.\n"}